From 5da2b4150e3f3b0739cd2bbde321efa70d6f763e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:41:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: OPTIONS-REGISTRY GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK - NaN FIXED,
 bit-identity NOT established

Rewrites the row against measured state and retracts three claims it carried.

Retracted 1: '=0 restores the exact pre-slot behaviour on every architecture.'
False on x86 - c7645a0df replaced the x86 Q2_0 vec_dot outside this toggle.

Retracted 2: the x86 Q2_0 vec_dot fast path 'is bit-exact with the scalar loop
it replaces, so it is an implementation, not an option.' Falsified; it carried
PrismML's g128 literals into a g64 tree.

Retracted 3: 'OFF emits no CPU_REPACK line at all and CPU_Mapped grows by the
same amount.' The first half holds, the second does not. CPU_Mapped measured
625.75 MiB in BOTH arms - the repack buffer is an additional allocation and the
mmap accounting is unchanged. The row's own prior numbers (322.28 + 95.98 ON vs
323.45 OFF) already contradicted it.

Recorded as achieved: NaN gone; engagement proven in both arms on two models
(CPU_REPACK 4.68 MiB and 95.98 MiB ON, no CPU_REPACK line OFF); ON and OFF now
token-identical over 32 tokens, deterministic 3/3 per arm; repaired path tracks
the unquantized fp16 reference.

Recorded as NOT achieved, and left open rather than rounded off: bit-identity.
First-token top-3 logprobs still differ by about 0.10, which is far larger than
FP32 summation-order rounding across ~76 blocks explains. Candidate cause noted
(activation quantisation via quantize_mat_q8_0 vs quantize_row_q8_0); owed a
later pass.

Performance stays UNMEASURED by the step gate, and two earlier figures are
marked void: the +58% decode and +354% prompt gaps came from a NaN-poisoned ON
arm, and any pre-2026-07-24 ON/OFF gap was measured against a baseline that
read out of bounds and issued twice the activation loads it should have.

Ported-mechanism: n/a - measurement record
